<section class="ph"><div class="ph-media"><img class="ph-img" src="/assets/img/photos/suburban-home.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/suburban-home-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/suburban-home.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap ph-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><a href="/mi-cities-served/">Cities</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span aria-current="page">Troy</span></nav><p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Metro Detroit · Oakland County</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in Troy, Michigan</h1><p class="ph-lede">Troy is Oakland County suburbia at its most established: curving subdivisions of colonials and ranches, plus the office towers and retail along Big Beaver Road. Its claims run from basement water to hail-damaged roofs on large homes.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-maize" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-glass" href="/request-claim-review/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="ph-facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Oakland County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Metro Detroit</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<div class="local"><div><p class="local-k">Neighborhoods &amp; areas</p><p>Big Beaver Road corridor, Somerset Collection area, Long Lake Road area, Square Lake Road area, Civic Center area, Rochester Road corridor</p></div><div><p class="local-k">Housing mix</p><p>Troy is mostly 1960s–1990s colonials, split-levels and ranches in planned subdivisions, with condos, newer custom homes and a large commercial and office district.</p></div><div><p class="local-k">Common claim drivers</p><ul class="chips"><li>Hail and wind</li><li>Basement flooding</li><li>Ice dams</li><li>Frozen pipes</li><li>Commercial roof leaks</li></ul></div></div>
<h2>Troy Homeowners and Businesses: Resolving Claim Disputes</h2>
<p>Troy’s subdivisions were mostly built from the 1960s onward, and many of those homes now have original or second-generation roofs, aging sump systems and finished basements. That makes hail, ice and water the most common sources of claims. Along Big Beaver Road and the Rochester Road corridor, office buildings and retail centers add commercial roof and water losses to the mix.</p>
<h3>Water in the basement</h3>
<p>The August 11, 2014 flood that swamped I-696 and much of southeast Oakland and Macomb counties sent water into basements across the region, and the late-June 2021 storms brought another round of flooded lower levels. In Troy, a finished basement can hold a family room, an office, a guest suite and a mechanical room. When water comes in through a failed sump pump or a floor drain backup, the estimate needs to cover drying, demolition, rebuilding and contents, not just carpet cleaning.</p>
<h3>Hail and the large-roof problem</h3>
<p>Colonials and custom homes in Troy often have large, steep roofs with multiple facets, valleys and dormers. Hail damage on one or two slopes can lead to a dispute about whether a full replacement is warranted, especially if the replacement shingles won’t match. These are amount-of-loss questions, and they are a good fit for appraisal. Our <a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/hail-roof-damage-appraisal/">hail and roof damage appraisal</a> service documents the damage and checks the estimate against what a proper repair requires.</p>
<h3>Commercial properties and associations</h3>
<p>Troy is home to many office buildings, retail centers and condominium associations. Large low-slope commercial roofs, rooftop equipment and shared building systems create complex claims, and condo associations must coordinate the master policy with individual owners. Disputes often come down to how much of a roof system needs replacement and what the restoration actually costs. See our <a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/commercial-condo-hoa-appraisal/">commercial, condo and HOA appraisal</a> page for how we approach larger losses.</p>
<p>Winter adds another layer. Large two-story colonials with complex rooflines are prone to ice dams along valleys and eaves, especially in years with heavy snow followed by a thaw. Water that works its way under the shingles can stain ceilings, soak insulation and damage interior finishes, and those losses are frequently disputed on scope rather than coverage.</p><p>Troy sits among Rochester Hills, Clawson, Birmingham and the Bloomfield area, and the same storm patterns affect the whole area. Whether you own a single-family home off Long Lake Road or manage a building near Big Beaver, the key is the same: a documented, line-by-line scope that reflects the real cost to repair.</p>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Percentage deductibles</b>Some policies, especially on higher-value homes and commercial buildings, use a deductible based on a percentage of the insured value. Know what yours is before you calculate the gap.</div>
<p>The <a href="/mi-claim-calculators/percentage-deductible-calculator/">percentage deductible calculator</a> shows how your deductible affects the amount actually in dispute.</p>
<h2>Services available in Troy</h2>
<p>Every Michigan Insurance Appraiser service is available to owners in Troy and surrounding communities, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Demand Representation</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/homeowner-claim-appraiser/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/commercial-condo-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial, Condo &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/hail-roof-damage-appraisal/">Hail &amp; Roof Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/windstorm-tornado-appraisal/">Windstorm &amp; Tornado Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/ice-dam-frozen-pipe-appraisal/">Ice Dam &amp; Frozen Pipe Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/water-sewer-backup-appraisal/">Water &amp; Sewer Backup Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/fire-smoke-loss-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Loss Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Questions from Troy property owners</h2><div class="qa"><details><summary><span>Do you handle commercial claims in Troy?</span><i class="qa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>Yes. We review estimates and serve as appraisers on office, retail and multi-family losses, as well as condo and HOA claims.</p></div></details><details><summary><span>Will appraisal decide whether my whole roof is replaced?</span><i class="qa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>Appraisal sets the amount of loss. If the evidence shows a full replacement is needed to repair the covered damage, that cost can be part of the award. Whether matching is required is a policy question.</p></div></details></div>
